---
import DocPage from "../../layouts/DocPage.astro";

const title = "sf-intelligence vs Elements.cloud - sf-intelligence";
const description =
  "Compare sf-intelligence with Elements.cloud: free offline MCP + local graph vs enterprise Change Intelligence, Conversational Org Intelligence, and a coming Metadata MCP.";

const jsonld = [
  {
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    mainEntity: [
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        name: "What is the difference between sf-intelligence and Elements.cloud?",
        acceptedAnswer: {
          "@type": "Answer",
          text: "Elements.cloud is an enterprise, cloud-hosted Change Intelligence platform (managed package + web app) with Conversational Org Intelligence and a Metadata MCP server targeted for Spring 2026. sf-intelligence is a free, open-source, offline, read-only MCP server that keeps a confidence-tagged metadata graph on your machine.",
        },
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        name: "Does Elements.cloud have an MCP server?",
        acceptedAnswer: {
          "@type": "Answer",
          text: "Elements publicly markets a Metadata MCP server (targeted Spring 2026) so external AI clients can use their org model. That means 'MCP access to dependency-aware org intelligence' is no longer unique to sf-intelligence — the remaining contrasts are offline/local processing, free licensing, source availability, and honesty-labeled edges.",
        },
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        name: "Does sf-intelligence send my Salesforce metadata to a cloud?",
        acceptedAnswer: {
          "@type": "Answer",
          text: "No. sf-intelligence builds a local vault with one read-only retrieve and then answers offline by default. Elements.cloud stores org metadata in its service to power dashboards and conversational analysis.",
        },
      },
    ],
  },
];
---

<DocPage
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path="/compare/elements-cloud"
  heading="sf-intelligence vs Elements.cloud"
  intro="Elements.cloud is the closest <strong>enterprise</strong> peer: same class of questions (impact, debt, process), hosted. sf-intelligence is the free local MCP. This page is fair about overlap — including their Conversational Org Intelligence and MCP roadmap."
  crumbs={[
    { label: "compare", href: "/compare" },
    { label: "vs Elements.cloud", href: "/compare/elements-cloud" },
  ]}
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: "Compare", path: "/compare" },
    { name: "vs Elements.cloud", path: "/compare/elements-cloud" },
  ]}
  jsonld={jsonld}
>
  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="prose">
        <div class="callout">
          <p><strong>Short answer:</strong> If you need a shared governance dashboard, BA/process maps, and a vendor SLA, Elements.cloud is built for that. If you need free, local, read-only org context for AI agents — with confidence labels and no metadata upload — that's sf-intelligence. Once Elements' MCP ships, both can sit in the same agent client; pick on trust model and cost.</p>
        </div>

        <h2 id="summary">At a glance</h2>
        <table class="doc-table">
          <thead><tr><th>&nbsp;</th><th>sf-intelligence</th><th>Elements.cloud</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>Category</strong></td><td>Offline MCP server + CLI</td><td>Enterprise Change Intelligence platform</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Delivery</strong></td><td>Local npm package</td><td>Cloud SaaS (managed package + web app)</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Where metadata lives</strong></td><td><strong>Your machine</strong></td><td>Vendor cloud</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Cost</strong></td><td>Free (MIT + Commons Clause)</td><td>Commercial SaaS (plans / trial on their site)</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Open source</strong></td><td>Yes</td><td>No</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Works offline</strong></td><td>Yes — after one retrieve</td><td>No — cloud service</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Conversational org AI</strong></td><td>Via your MCP host + sfi tools</td><td>Conversational Org Intelligence (2026 rollout)</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>MCP for external agents</strong></td><td>Native today</td><td>Metadata MCP targeted Spring 2026</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Primary user</strong></td><td>Developers &amp; AI coding agents</td><td>Architects, platform owners, governance</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Process mapping / BA</strong></td><td>Limited / generated docs</td><td>Core platform (process maps, requirements)</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Dependency / impact</strong></td><td>Yes — local graph</td><td>Yes — core platform feature</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>

        <h2 id="when-sfi">Choose sf-intelligence when you want to…</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Keep metadata on the machine and audit the code yourself</li>
          <li>Pay $0 and live in Claude Code / Cursor</li>
          <li>Get confidence / provenance labels on heuristic findings</li>
          <li>Run a local <a href="/use-cases/agent-readiness-audit">agent-readiness</a> pass without a SaaS contract</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="when-elements">Choose Elements.cloud when you want to…</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>A shared web dashboard and enterprise change-governance workflows</li>
          <li>Business-analysis tooling (process maps, requirements traceability)</li>
          <li>Vendor-supported managed package and team collaboration</li>
          <li>Their conversational engine + upcoming MCP against an already-ingested cloud model</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="together">Complementary</h2>
        <p>Teams can keep Elements as the system-of-record for governance while developers use sf-intelligence for day-to-day editor questions. The security distinction that matters is still <strong>where metadata lives</strong>.</p>

        <h2 id="more">More comparisons</h2>
        <p><a href="/compare">compare hub</a> · <a href="/compare/salesforce-dx-mcp">Salesforce MCP</a> · <a href="/compare/dx0">dx0</a> · <a href="/compare/hubbl">Hubbl</a> · <a href="/compare/metazoa">Metazoa</a> · <a href="/compare/sweep">Sweep</a>.</p>

        <div class="callout"><p><strong>Disclaimer:</strong> Public positioning as of mid-2026; verify Elements' current MCP status and pricing on their site. sf-intelligence is independent — not affiliated with Elements.cloud or Salesforce.</p></div>

        <div style="padding-top:36px;">
          <div class="cta-box">
            <h2 class="screen-type">Free, local, read-only.</h2>
            <p>Same class of questions — on your machine, in your editor.</p>
            <div class="cta-actions">
              <a class="btn btn-solid" href="/getting-started">install sf-intelligence</a>
              <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/ai-safety">is AI safe on my org?</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</DocPage>
